project/landing-themetoggle-crumb-slot: spoint client/landing/index.html theme toggle belongs in the kit-native Crumb `right` slot (C.Crumb({trail,leaf,right:C.ThemeToggle({compact:true})})), NOT injected into an absolute-positioned .lp-theme-slot over the Topbar — the overlay overlapped the nav links at every viewport (slotOverlapsNav=true mobile+desktop, witnessed local+deployed). General rule: the anentrypoint-design kit chrome (Topbar/Crumb/Status/AppShell) provides slots (Crumb.right, Topbar.search, Status.left/right); use the slot, never hand-position chrome with bespoke absolute CSS over it. Also: the kit ThemeToggle drives theme via its own applyTheme controller (theme.js) — do NOT keep a competing landing-local prefers-color-scheme script that sets data-theme directly; two controllers fight. Removed both. Witnessed at 390/768/1280/1440 + deployed: overlapsNav=false, toggle cycles data-theme through kit controller.